-- title:
--   Invariance of cusp sums under conjugation by GL₂⁺(ℝ)
-- statement:
--   Let $\Gamma',\Gamma''$ be subgroups of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$, each of finite index, with $-1\in\Gamma'$. Let $g\in\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$ have positive determinant, and let $e\colon\Gamma'\to\Gamma''$ be a group isomorphism such that for every $\gamma\in\Gamma'$ the relation [`ModularCurve.Period.conjRel`](def/ModularCurve_PeriodTransfer.html#L19) holds for $g$, $\gamma$ and $e(\gamma)$, i.e. $g\cdot\iota(\gamma)=\iota(e(\gamma))\cdot g$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$, where $\iota$ denotes the map `Matrix.SpecialLinearGroup.mapGL` from $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ into $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$; so $e$ is conjugation by $g$. Let $F\colon\Gamma''\to\mathbb{Q}$ be invariant under $\Gamma''$-conjugation at elements of trace $\pm2$: $F(\delta p\delta^{-1})=F(p)$ whenever $p,\delta\in\Gamma''$ and $\operatorname{tr}(p)^2=4$. For a finite-index subgroup $\Phi$, [`ModularCurve.PDPairing.cuspSum`](def/ModularCurve_PDPairing.html#L574) of a function on $\Phi$ is the sum, over the orbits $q$ of the group generated by $T=\begin{pmatrix}1&1\\0&1\end{pmatrix}$ acting on $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})/\Phi$, of its value at the cusp generator $x_q^{-1}T^{w_q}x_q\in\Phi$, where $x_q$ is the chosen lift to $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ of the chosen coset representative of $q$ and $w_q$ is the minimal period of $T$ acting on that coset. The conclusion is that the cusp sum of $F\circ e$ over $\Gamma'$ equals the cusp sum of $F$ over $\Gamma''$.
--
--   This is the transport of cusp data under conjugation by an element of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$ of positive determinant: such a conjugation matches the cusps of $\Gamma'$ with those of $\Gamma''$, carrying cusp generators to cusp generators up to $\Gamma''$-conjugacy, so that sums over cusps of conjugation-invariant functions on parabolic elements agree. It is used in the comparison of period pairings, [`ModularCurve.CupPairing.pair_comp_eq_of_conjRel`](thm.html#ModularCurve.CupPairing.pair_comp_eq_of_conjRel), and rests on the normal form of elements of trace $\pm2$ given by [`ModularGroup.exists_eq_conj_T_zpow_of_trace_sq_eq_four`](thm.html#ModularGroup.exists_eq_conj_T_zpow_of_trace_sq_eq_four).
